You must specify the data source name and type (metrics, logs, traces) upon creation.
The name of the data source will then be used as reference to name the associated Grafana data source.

USAGE:
  scw cockpit data-source create [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  [project-id]                                               Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  name                                                       Data source name
  type                                                       Data source type (unknown_type | metrics | logs | traces)
  [retention-days]                                           Duration for which the data will be retained in the data source
  [metrics-limits.ingestion-rate-limit-samples-per-second]   Maximum number of samples ingested per second
  [metrics-limits.max-series]                                Maximum number of active series
  [logs-limits.ingestion-rate-limit-bytes-per-second]        Maximum number of bytes ingested per second
  [traces-limits.ingestion-rate-limit-bytes-per-second]      Maximum number of bytes ingested per second
  [region=fr-par]                                            Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par | nl-ams | pl-waw | it-mil)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for create
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

SEE ALSO:
  # Generate a data source configuration snippet
  scw cockpit config get
